A process runs the following program in a multiprogramming system. A process enters the I/O queue whenever it performs an I/O operation, and a context switch happens whenever it requests I/O and whenever it returns from I/O. There is no other cause of context switches. Not counting the first time the process is run, how many times does it enter the ready queue during its lifetime?

int main() {
   int a, b, i;
   scanf("%d", &a);
   scanf("%d", &b);
   for (i = 0; i < 12; i++) {
      a = a + b;
      printf("%d", a);
   }
   printf("done");
   return 0;
}

